{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792492184,"nonce":"s7mHbaLZ2u6YyVkpncCFfsHWF+o=","message":"Implemented the motion-background slice. Push records whether its owner is the dynamic batch; Pop returns to that saved owner even if the current route has changed. Layer command count snapshots use the same batch, so the existing CompositeBindingMeta index now reaches cached_dynamic_batch as apply_binding_deltas expects. Child primitive opacity excludes groups represented in that batch but preserves explicit opacity and groups from a different stream. Composite/foreground/image fallbacks remain unchanged.\n\nThe cached dynamic dispatcher now passes the complete batch, including paths and commands, without cloning the primitive vector. Both cached and public direct dispatch choose ordered single-sample composition for effect/opacity/3D groups, preserving the existing SDF coverage model. Ordinary batches retain direct render_overlay dispatch rather than gaining a viewport-sized intermediate pass. No timing benchmark has been run.\n\nNegative control before the fix on 09329da2: both new CPU ownership tests failed (local count 3 rather than 1 after an unrelated static group; Pop written into static instead of the saved motion owner). Both initial offscreen application cases failed: overlapping half-opacity red/green children produced [64,128,64,255] over blue rather than isolated-group [0,128,127,255]; the actual walker emitted four static commands instead of keeping only the two unrelated static commands. After the fix, the real walker/cached binding test patches opacity 0.5 -\u003e 0 -\u003e 0.75 -\u003e 0.25 without changing child alpha or static layer config. The public non-compositor path is checked too. A path-only nested-group fixture reaches the application overlay and retains quarter opacity. The no-effect opacity-1 endpoint stays correct on direct dispatch.\n\nReview also identified CSS records nested inside motion: apply_css_deltas still indexes the static cache. DrawContext now reports dynamic batch ownership and CssAnimPaintMeta retains it; that mixed case requests a full repaint before any static patch/re-emission can use foreign indices. The CSS dynamic-record guard has an offscreen application regression. This is a correctness fallback, not dynamic CSS in-place patch support. Composite scratch/CSS ownership and cross-stream group isolation remain in parent e0a7502e3e9d71bb983572df7db0033a67da1c48262e53368ae2399bc22e583a.\n\nFinal verification follows. One intermediate capability-probe run overlapped the new trait-method edits and compiled against a stale DrawContext dependency; it was not a data-texture shader failure. Capability overrides were restored and final probes run only after source edits are complete. Browser/mobile GPU pixels and timings remain unverified.","files":null}]}